# Library Management System

## Project Overview
The Library Management System is a database project built using PostgreSQL and Prisma ORM. It manages books, genres, and library users.

## Technologies Used
- Node.js
- TypeScript
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma ORM
- Prisma Client

## Database Models

### 1. User
Stores library user information, including:
- ID
- Name
- Email
- Role (PATRON or LIBRARIAN)
- Created date

### 2. Genre
Stores book categories and their relationships with books.

### 3. Book
Stores book information, including:
- ID
- Title
- Author
- ISBN
- Description
- Published year
- Genre relationship
- Created date

## Database Relationships
- One Genre can have many Books.
- Each Book belongs to one Genre.
- User roles are managed using a Role enum.

## Sample Data
The database is seeded with:
- 4 book genres
- 15 books

